phase-2 names of the germ-reading notions and theorems**, kept as aliases after the switch of
Definition 3.11 to the text's germ reading (phase 2, stage 2; Findings, Chapter 3, items 330–339).

# Phase-2 names (aliases)

## What is formalized

Nothing new.  During phase 2 the germ-reading notions were called `IsScFredholmGermG`,
`IsScFredholmSectionG`, `IsScFredholmGermTameG`, `IsScFredholmSectionTameG`, `IsGoodPositionGermG`,
`IsGoodPositionGermTameG`, `IsGoodPositionGermFilledG`, `IsGoodPositionGermScG` (files `*G.lean`),
and the germ-reading theorems `X_germ` (or `…G_…`).  At the switch the canonical names
(`IsScFredholmGerm`, `theorem_3_54`, …) were given to the germ reading, and the project's original
whole-chart notions and theorems were renamed `…WholeChart` / `…_wholeChart`.  This file keeps every
phase-2 name resolving: the eight notions as `abbrev`s, the theorems as `alias`es (generated by
script from the rename map of the switch, `stage2_renames.tsv`).

## What the text leaves implicit, and the choices made

* The old whole-chart names that now denote the germ reading need no alias: they resolve, to the
  statement with the text's hypotheses.  Only the names of the `*G.lean` / `Germ*.lean` files that
  were renamed away are listed here.
-/

noncomputable section

